cture**: $12.1B record backlog, ~$6B slated for 2027+, providing unprecedented near-term visibility [Actual \u2014 Q2'26 call].\n2. **Data-center AI cooling is a structural demand shift**, not just a cycle: Applied bookings +130% 4 consecutive quarters; hyperscaler capex forecast ~$1T by 2027 [Estimate \u2014 Moody's].\n3. **Services mix**: 1/3 of revenue growing low-teens CAGR since 2020; recurring revenue creates visibility that typical industrials lack [Actual \u2014 Q2'26 call].\n\n## 1.5-3. Base-rate shock check\n\n- My base case assumes 5-year revenue CAGR of ~6.6% (FY26-FY30), which exceeds the ~2-3% industrial base rate by **~2.2x**.\n- **RED FLAG triggered.** Note this explicitly: the forecast already embeds above-base-rate performance. If the data-center cycle breaks, the downward scenario is severe (20% scenario, $202/share bear case).\n\n---\n\n# SECTION 2. BUSINESS QUALITY\n\n## 2-1. Business Understanding (3 sentences)\n\nTrane Technologies designs, manufactures, sells, and services commercial and residential HVAC equipment (chillers, rooftops, heat pumps, controls) primarily in the Americas, EMEA, and Asia-Pacific. The company generates ~1/3 of revenue from high-margin recurring services (maintenance, parts, controls) on its installed base of millions of units. TT is currently experiencing a demand super-cycle in data-center liquid and air-cooled thermal management, with bookings +37% and a record backlog of $12.1B.\n\n**Understandability: HIGH**\n\n## 2-2. Moat Assessment + Dynamics\n\n| Moat type | Score (0-3) | Direction | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Intangible assets (brand) | 3 | Widening | Trane is a 100+ yr premium brand; innovation leadership in efficient chillers |\n| Switching costs | 3 | Stable | Installed base lock-in; proprietary controls and service contracts |\n| Network effects | 0 | \u2014 | Not material |\n| Cost advantage | 1 | Stable | Scale benefits but not lowest-cost |\n| Economies of scale | 2 | Widening | 4x applied capacity expansion in 3 years [Actual \u2014 Q2'26] |\n| Regulatory barriers | 2 | Widening | Energy efficiency mandates (SEER, building codes) favor premium equipment |\n| Data moat | 1 | Widening | Agentic AI / connected building data improves efficiency analytics |\n\n**Total: 12/21 \u2014 WIDE moat** | **Direction: Widening**\n\n## 2-3. Lynch Classification\n\n**Fast Grower with Stalwart characteristics** (growth >15% EPS in 2026, but services give durability). Checkpoints are:\n- Balance sheet: Net debt/EBITDA ~0.8x \u2192 PASS\n- FCF generation: $2.75B after SBC \u2192 PASS\n- Defensible growth: AI cooling + services \u2192 PASS\n- Valuation (Lynch would say PEG >1.5-2.0 is interesting but his rule of thumb fails here): PEG trailing 1.95 \u2192 borderline FAIL (premium)\n\n## 2-4. Financial Strength Scorecard\n\n| Metric | Value | Tag |\n|---|---|---|\n| Revenue CAGR (5yr trailing) | 11.3% | [Actual \u2014 pack] |\n| Operating margin (latest FY) | 18.6% | [Actual \u2014 arithmetic] |\n| Operating margin (median 12yr) | 12.5% | [Actual \u2014 pack] |\n| ROE (vendor) | 36.6% | [Aggregator] |\n| ROIC (adjusted, est.) | ~19% | [Estimate \u2014 Layer 2.5] |\n| FCF margin | 13.3% (FY25) | [Estimate \u2014 /revenue] |\n| FCF conversion (FCF/OCF) | 88.1% | [Estimate \u2014 /OCF] |\n| Net debt / EBITDA | ~0.85x | [Estimate] |\n| Net cash position | Negative (net debt ~$3.7B incl. leases) | [Estimate] |\n| Interest coverage | >18x | [Estimate \u2014 $3.97B op inc / $0.227B int] |\n\n**Judgment: EXCELLENT**\n\n## 2-5. Capital Allocation Scorecard (0-15)\n\n| Criteria | Score (0-3) | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| Buyback efficiency | 3 | $840M YTD 2026, $3.8B remaining; share count shrinking ~1.5%/yr [Actual \u2014 Q2'26 call + pack] |\n| M&A track record | 2 | Stellar ($500M rev target 2026) early days; history of disciplined tuck-ins |\n| Capex efficiency | 3 | 2-3% of revenue = asset-light; returns >20% on incremental capex |\n| Mix rationality | 3 | Balance of growth capex 