 vs 19.5% \u2192 \u00b1$15 \u2014 KPI: Segment mix/services growth\nAlso note: if WACC falls to 7.5% (market-implied), IV = ~$400 \u2014 see Reverse DCF below.\n\nStep 3-6. Reverse DCF (what the market believes)\nAt $453.43, the market implies either (a) a ~7.0\u20137.5% equity discount rate with my FCF path, or (b) 2032 owner-FCF \u2248 $8.5\u20139.0B / EPS \u2248 $38\u201340 (\u224815% EPS CAGR for a decade) \u2014 i.e., the data-center bull case becomes the BASE case. Feasible, but NOT verifiable from current disclosures.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 3.5 \u2014 SECOND-ORDER EFFECTS\n\nStep 3.5-1. Competitive response\nIf TT's data-center applied strategy keeps winning (130% bookings growth, 4x capacity), Vertiv, Modine, Carrier, and JCI will expand aggressively; hyperscalers will multi-source and force price convergence. Nvidia's rack-architecture choices can reset the game (CES 2026 comments rattled cooling stocks \u2014 this event is [Actual]). Net impact: \u22121 (competition will compress applied margins over time).\n\nStep 3.5-2. Reflexivity\nPositive: high share price \u2192 cheap M&A currency (Stellar), customer confidence (critical for 5-year service contracts), talent attraction. Negative: a derating would have mild effects given SBC is only 0.4% of revenue. Reflexivity is positive but contained.\n\nStep 3.5-3. Customer behavior\nHyperscalers are sophisticated, procurement-driven buyers \u2014 switching costs are moderate in equipment, high in service/controls. As AI cooling moves from early adopters to mainstream, equipment margins will normalize toward standard chiller economics; the durable value is in the services annuity (~1/3 of revenue).\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 4 \u2014 SCENARIOS (BAYESIAN)\n\nStep 4-1/2. Scenarios (probabilities sum to 100%; base is the modal case)\n- BEAR (25%): AI-capex digestion; applied bookings normalize from +130% to +10%; residential stays weak; 10Y >5.25%. Revenue growth fades to 3% by 2029; OPM peaks at 19%; WACC 9.5%. IV \u2248 $230/share [Estimate].\n- BASE (50%): As Section 3. Revenue $34.8B by 2032; OPM 21%; WACC 8.75%. IV \u2248 $310\u2013330/share \u2192 $312 [Estimate].\n- BULL (25%): TT captures ~15\u201320% of the 27%-CAGR liquid-cooling TAM; organic growth 11\u201312% through 2028; services grows low-teens; margins 21.5%; WACC 8.5%. IV \u2248 $350\u2013360/share [Estimate]. (Analyst mean PT $525 requires an additional rerating to ~35x \u2014 beyond my bull's DCF.)\n\nStep 4-3. Bayesian update\n- Prior (base rate of mega-cap industrial sustaining >8% growth for a decade): ~35% [Assumption].\n- Evidence: backlog +70%, bookings +37%, guidance raised twice, applied +130% \u00d74 quarters [Actual].\n- Posterior: ~50% [Estimate]. My base+bull = 75% \u2014 at the 1.5x base-rate cap; the delta is justified only by the backlog/services/regulatory evidence above. Flag accepted.\n\nStep 4-4/5. Expected value and margin of safety\nExpected value = 0.25\u00d7230 + 0.50\u00d7312 + 0.25\u00d7350 = $301\n50% CI: $285\u2013$345 | 80% CI: $230\u2013$400\nMargin of safety (base vs T0): (312 \u2212 453.43)/312 = \u221245.3% \u2014 NONE (negative)\nMargin of safety (EV vs T0): (301 \u2212 453.43)/301 = \u221250.6% \u2014 NONE\n3-year scenario target: Bear $230 / Base $345 / Bull $480; E[P\u2083] = $350 \u2192 expected 3-yr CAGR = (350/453)^(1/3) \u2212 1 = \u22128.2%/yr [Arithmetic].\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 4.5 \u2014 TIME-HORIZON ARBITRAGE\n\n- Market-implied horizon: at 29.7x FY26E and ~26x FY27E, the market is capitalizing ~6\u20138 years of high-teens EPS growth. The market horizon \u2248 6\u20138 years.\n- My horizon: 3\u20135 years (the period over which backlog and guidance provide visibility).\n- Spread = \u22121 to \u22123 years (negative arbitrage): at this price, the market's horizon is LONGER than any evidence base I can verify. No arbitrage opportunity in my favor.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 5 \u2014 CONVICTION & POSITION SIZING\n\nStep 5-1. Conviction score (0\u20133 each; total /15)\n1. Business quality: 3 (fortress moat, ROIC 25%+, Piotroski 8/8, OCF/NI TTM 133%)\n2. Valuation attractiveness: 1 (MoS \u221245% vs base; 30x forward vs ~25x historical top)\n3. Macro alignment: 2 (reflation dominant; modest rate headwind for a 30x multiple)\n4. Thesis clarity: 3 (bookings, backlog, applied growth, service CAGR \u2014 all measurable)\n5. Execution traceability: 3 (12-yr record, raised guidance twice, capital allocation 13/15)\nTOTAL: 12/15 \u2192 HIGH\nAdjustments: macro headwind \u22120.5; red-team logic gap <2 \u2192 \u22120.5 (per Layer 9). Effective conviction: 11/15 (High).\n0.5-step conviction decay applies automatically for any hold >6 months without new confirmatory evidence.\n\nStep 5-3. Sizing guideline\nHigh conviction normally suggests 4\u20136%. The negative MoS overrides: NEW MONEY WEIGHT = 0%. Existing holders: trim toward 2\u20133% (from 4\u20135%).\nEntry/re-entry zone: $310\u2013350 (base IV range); aggressive add <$290.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 5.5 \u2014 BEHAVIORAL & POSITIONING\n\n- Short interest: 1.91% of float; DTC 3.31; MoM \u22129.5% [Actual vendor, stale 8/10/26] \u2192 no squeeze fuel; no bearish hedge anywhere.\n- Institutional ownership: 91.6%; insider 0.27% [Actual vendor] \u2192 extremely crowded; flows are ETF/index-driven, not fundamental.\n- Sell-side: 13 Buy / 0 Sell / 11 Hold (21 analysts) [Estimate - Investing.com snippet]; mean PT $525.28, median $532 [Actual pack, stale 8/10/26] \u2192 bullish tilt near-zero bearish dissent.\n- Momentum: stock +21% in 30 days, near 52-wk high $505.87 [Estimate - TIKR/pack].\n- Crowding risk score: 11/15. Deduct \u22121%p from target weight (already 0 for new money).\n- Interpretation: the crowd is uniformly long; there is no contrarian lift. This is a classic late-stage quality-momentum setup \u2014 great business, wrong risk-reward.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 6 \u2014 PORTFOLIO FIT\n\n- In a diversified quality-growth portfolio, TT is now a proxy for the AI-capex trade (correlated with NVDA, VRT, MOD, CARR in drawdowns). Its standalone quality is excellent, but at 30x forward the marginal portfolio contribution is negative expected return.\n- Common bear triggers: AI-capex digestion, 10Y >5.25%, commercial-construction freeze. Position should be trimmed to a level where a 30% drawdown is tolerable (2\u20133% weight).\n- Rotation candidates: cheaper quality with less rate duration (financials, value industrials) \u2014 consistent with Reflation regime.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 6.5 \u2014 KELLY SIZING\n\n- Scenario 3-yr payoffs: Bear $230 (25%), Base $345 (50%), Bull $480 (25%). E[P\u2083] = $350; expected return \u22128.2%/yr.\n- Kelly fraction: negative for any long position (expected excess return < 0). f* = 0.0%.\n- Long-only constraint: new weight = 0%; for existing holders, trim.\n- Layer 5 vs 6.5 gap: 4\u20136% vs 0% = 4\u20136pp \u2014 inside the 20pp re-analysis threshold, but the conclusion is the same: valuation destroys the case for adding.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 7 \u2014 RISKS & CATALYSTS\n\nRisks (probability-weighted impact):\n1. AI-capex cycle normalizes; applied bookings revert (High/Medium-High impact) \u2014 leading indicator: hyperscaler capex guidance, Nvidia architecture decisions.\n2. 10Y breaks 5.25% \u2192 de-rating of the 30x multiple (Medium impact).\n3. Applied margin erosion as hyperscalers multi-source (Vertiv, Modine, Carrier) (Medium).\n4. Residential HVAC stays weak; Middle East/EMEA disruption (Low-Medium).\n5. Stellar integration under-delivers (Low).\nCatalysts:\n1. Q3'26: organic rev ~10%, adjusted EPS ~$4.70 [Actual - company guidance].\n2. Continued applied bookings >+100% YoY; backlog >$12B.\n3. Transport refrigeration recovery late 2026 [Actual - company].\n4. Rate cuts \u2192 multiple expansion.\n5. Buyback: $840M YTD, $3.8B remaining [Actual - company].\n\nPre-Mortem (Layer 7-4): If TT fails by 2030, the cause will be one of: (1) AI-cooling architecture shifts away from TT's strengths (NVDA CES event as precursor); (2) rates >5.5% for 2 years crushing commercial construction; (3) a price war in liquid cooling led by Vertiv/Modine/Carrier; (4) services growth stalling once equipment share falters. Early-warning indicators: applied bookings <+30% YoY for two quarters; backlog <$8B; data-center vertical growth <10%; OPM <18.5%; service growth <8%.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 7.5 \u2014 CORRELATION-ADJUSTED RISK\n\n- Tail correlation: TT's AI-cooling driver has >0.8 correlation with VRT/MOD/CARR/NVDA in AI-capex shocks [Assumption].\n- Common bear trigger across a quality-growth portfolio: AI-capex digestion + rate repricing (2022 playbook).\n- Conditional VaR (5%): in a 2022-style derating of the AI complex, a 30x-multiple stock with an 8.8% owner-FCF yield-like profile could fall ~30\u201340% from $453 \u2192 $270\u2013315 within two quarters [Estimate]. TT's fundamentals would be intact; the multiple would compress.\n- Mitigation: cap TT weight at 2\u20133% and keep the re-entry list ready.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 8 \u2014 MONITORING RULES (THESIS INTEGRITY)\n\nThresholds that trigger re-evaluation:\n1. Applied bookings YoY: warn <+30%; thesis break <+10% for two quarters.\n2. Total backlog: maintain >$10B; warn <$8B; confirm $6B 2027+ conversion on schedule.\n3. Service revenue growth: >10%; warn <8%.\n4. Q3'26 actuals (due Oct 2026): organic revenue \u226510%, adjusted EPS \u2265$4.70, FY26 adjusted EPS \u2265$15.20.\n5. OPM: \u226519% FY26; \u226520% FY27.\n6. Owner-FCF (OCF \u2212 capex \u2212 SBC): \u2265$2.9B FY26.\n7. Buybacks: \u2265$1.5B annual run-rate.\n8. 10Y >5.25%: reassess WACC and target multiple.\n9. Price triggers: BUILD at \u2264$345; ADD at \u2264$290; TRIM further at >$500; SELL outright on any two thesis-break thresholds.\n10. Request from IR: separate disclosure of data-center revenue and backlog.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 9 \u2014 RED TEAM & ADVERSARIAL ANALYSIS\n\nStep 9-1. Short thesis (same data, hostile framing)\n- The market pays 35.7x trailing / 29.7x forward for a company whose 12-yr median OPM was 12.5% \u2014 a cyclical equipment maker wearing a compounder's clothes.\n- Applied bookings +130% for four quarters is PULLING FORWARD demand; a 2-yr stack of 4x applied bookings means the comps are mathematically brutal by 2027.\n- Data-center liquid cooling TAM is only $4.8B in 2025 (27% CAGR \u2192 $14.8B by 2030); even a dominant TT share adds only ~$2\u20133B revenue by 2030 \u2014 already fully priced at $453.\n- Residential is weak; EMEA Middle East \u221230%; transport hasn't turned \u2014 the entire story is one vertical in one region: Americas commercial/data-center.\n- Nvidia's architecture choices are a binary risk; CES comments already rattled the group once.\n- Stellar is EPS-neutral with \"reinvestment\" \u2014 M&A dilution dressed as strategy.\n- Record backlog means future growth is KNOWN; the buy-side crowds into certainty at peak multiples (short interest 1.91% = nobody hedges).\n- At 4.71% 10Y, the long-duration multiple (30x) is vulnerable to any inflation re-acceleration.\n\nStep 9-2. Logic combat\nLong logic: 6.5/10 (quality, backlog, regulation, services annuity are real; valuation is the flaw).\nShort logic: 5.5/10 (timing-dependent; a fortress-moat company with a 12-month backlog can stay expensive for years; shorting it risks 30\u201350% squeezes).\nGap = 1.0 < 2.0 \u2192 conviction downgrade of 0.5 step (already applied in Section 5).\n\nStep 9-3. Adversarial data\nNo active Hindenburg-style short report on TT was found in the research window [Unconfirmed]. Risk factors: legal/regulatory exposure listed as TT's top risk category (28 risks) [Estimate - TipRanks snippet]; activist angle absent.\n\nStep 9-4. Killed arguments (and the conditions that would revive them)\n- \"Data-center revenue is immaterial\" \u2014 KILLED by applied bookings +130% / $6B 2027 backlog. REVIVES if applied bookings <+30%.\n- \"Rates don't matter for quality\" \u2014 KILLED by history (2022 halved quality multiples). REVIVES if 10Y >5.25%.\n- \"TT is a bond proxy at 30x\" \u2014 KILLED by arithmetic: at 30x, a 9% grower is NOT a bond proxy. REVIVES below 20x.\n- \"The analyst $525 mean proves upside\" \u2014 KILLED by base rates (analyst targets lag price; 0 sell-side bears = sentiment extreme). REVIVES if guidance is again raised and 10Y declines.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u25